From: Nuxel <nuxel@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] nfc: sec_nfc: do not gate the NFC reader on the eSE/TEE state

On SM-G975F (beyond2lte) the S3NRN82 NFC controller at I2C 0x27 is healthy,
but /dev/sec-nfc cannot be opened.  CONFIG_ESE_SECURE makes sec_nfc_open()
call tz_tee_ese_secure_check(); the TEE on this image reports the embedded
Secure Element (eSE, Samsung Pay) is not secured and the vendor driver then
returns -EBUSY, so the NFC reader is disabled by an unrelated payment check.

Nuxel does not support payment/eSE.  Record the eSE as "not secured"
without invoking the TEE (measured: the TEE call result 0xffff000d also
reaches the kernel open path as a bogus pointer and panics with oops=panic)
and keep the NFC reader usable.  An eSE consumer must still consult
nfc_ese_secured itself, so no payment functionality is enabled.

Also reject an open without driver data instead of dereferencing NULL.

Signed-off-by: Nuxel <nuxel@localhost>
---
 drivers/nfc/sec_nfc.c | 30 +++++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/nfc/sec_nfc.c
+++ b/drivers/nfc/sec_nfc.c
@@ -644,21 +644,28 @@
 
 	NFC_LOG_INFO("%s\n", __func__);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_ESE_SECURE
-	if (nfc_ese_secured == NOT_CHECKED) {
-		ret = tz_tee_ese_secure_check();
-		if (ret) {
-			nfc_ese_secured = ESE_NOT_SECURED;
-			NFC_LOG_ERR("eSE spi is not Secured\n"); 
-			return -EBUSY;
-		}
-		nfc_ese_secured = ESE_SECURED;
-	} else if (nfc_ese_secured == ESE_NOT_SECURED) { 
-		NFC_LOG_ERR("eSE spi is not Secured\n"); 
-		return -EBUSY;
-	}
+	/*
+	 * NUXEL (SM-G975F, beyond2lte): the TEE eSE check gates the *embedded
+	 * Secure Element* (Samsung Pay / payment), not the NFC reader.  The TEE
+	 * on this Nuxel image reports the eSE is not secured, and the vendor
+	 * driver then refuses to open the *NFC* misc device at all.  Nuxel does
+	 * not support payment/eSE, so the eSE state is recorded as "not
+	 * secured" without invoking the TEE (the call also trips the kernel
+	 * open path on this image, see nfc3.md), and the NFC reader stays
+	 * usable.  Any eSE consumer must check nfc_ese_secured itself.
+	 */
+	if (nfc_ese_secured == NOT_CHECKED)
+		nfc_ese_secured = ESE_NOT_SECURED;
+	if (nfc_ese_secured == ESE_NOT_SECURED)
+		NFC_LOG_DBG("NUXEL: eSE not secured; NFC reader path continues\n");
 #endif
+
+	if (!info) {
+		NFC_LOG_ERR("NUXEL: open() without driver data\n");
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
 
 	mutex_lock(&info->mutex);
 	if (info->mode != SEC_NFC_MODE_OFF) {
 		NFC_LOG_ERR("open() nfc is busy\n");
